@title Course Portal Single Sign-On
@subtitle Kestrel Learning platform team. Version dated 2026-10-08

# Sign-in sequence

diagram sso sequence title="Sign-in sequence"
sso: br "Browser" user
sso: portal "Course Portal" svc
sso: idp "Identity Provider" svc
sso: tok "Token Service" svc
sso: dir "User Directory" db
sso: audit "Audit Log" store
sso: br -> portal : open /courses
sso: portal --> br : redirect to Identity Provider
sso: br -> idp : authorization request with PKCE
sso: idp -> dir : verify credentials and groups
sso: dir --> idp : verified, groups returned
sso: idp -> tok : issue tokens
sso: tok --> idp : tokens issued
sso: idp --> br : redirect with one-time code
sso: br -> portal : one-time code
sso: portal -> tok : exchange code for tokens
sso: tok -> audit : record sign-in
sso: portal --> br : session cookie, 24 hours

# Token lifetimes

table = Token,Lifetime; ID token,10 minutes; Access token,30 minutes; Refresh token,8 hours; Session cookie,24 hours; One-time code,60 seconds

!! A one-time code expires after 60 seconds and works only once.

# Rules

- Staff accounts must pass MFA.
- A one-time code can be used once only.
- Sign-in events are kept for 400 days.
